module

public import Theory.GroupTheory.Recognition.HeldM22A10.LocalStructure

/-!
# Held's M22/A10 recognition: local setup and preliminary structure

This interface exposes the exact local input and its elementary consequences:
the involution centralizer has order 384 and center generated by the given
involution, and the chosen ambient Sylow two-subgroup has order 128.

Source: Huppert--Blackburn, *Finite Groups III*, XII, 1.18(b), printed p.314;
D. Held, "Eine Kennzeichnung der Mathieu-Gruppe M22 und der alternierenden
Gruppe A10", J. Algebra 8 (1968), 436--449, DOI 10.1016/0021-8693(68)90054-9.
The book also cites Z. Janko, "A characterization of the Mathieu simple groups",
I and II, J. Algebra 9 (1968), 1--19 and 20--41.

The splitting of the centralizer over its elementary normal subgroup and the
global equivalence with the concrete M22 or A10 remain to be proved. No global
recognition theorem is asserted by this interface yet.
-/
